Main code compiles. Now write tests. Two test classes:

1. `PalletFlowTest` — main flow, failure branches, idempotency, recall→pending review, history time range, persistence.
2. `PalletConcurrencyTest` — concurrent load same batch, ship vs unload, same command replay.

Also update existing tests' cleanTables to delete new tables.

PalletFlowTest helpers:
- unique()
- createPallet(palletKey, dividers, expected) → posts {"commandKey":"CK-P-...","palletKey":...,"dividerCount":n}
- createBatch(batchKey, items, expected) — same as BatchFlowTest pattern
- submitTest, approve, recall helpers for batch flow
- load(palletKey, commandKey, items...) — build JSON body
- loadRaw(palletKey, body, expected)
- unload(palletKey, commandKey, keys, expected)
- ship(palletKey, commandKey, expected)
- dispose(palletKey, commandKey, reason, expected)
- getDetail/getHistory/getDiagnostics returning JsonNode

Let me write the tests carefully.

Test 1: happyFlow_loadUnloadShipSnapshotAndDisposal
```java
String pallet = "PL-HAPPY-" + unique();
String b1 = "BK-PH1-" + unique(); b2, b3
createPallet(pallet, 2, 201);
createBatch(b1, List.of("t1"), 201); ... b2, b3
// load: b1 catA comp1, b2 catA comp1, b3 catB comp2
MvcResult loadResult = load(pallet, "CK-L-1", items(item(b1,"A",1), item(b2,"A",1), item(b3,"B",2)), 201);
JsonNode loadBody = read(loadResult);
assertEquals(3, loadBody.path("items").size());
assertEquals(1, loadBody.path("dividerVersion").asInt());
// detail
JsonNode detail = getJson("/api/pallets/" + pallet);
assertEquals(3, detail.path("currentLoads").size());
assertTrue(detail.path("shipment").isNull() or isMissingNode);
// diagnostics
JsonNode diag = getJson("/api/pallets/" + pallet + "/diagnostics");
assertEquals(2, diag.path("actualDividers").asInt());
assertEquals(1, diag.path("requiredDividers").asInt());
assertEquals(0, diag.path("dividerDeficit").asInt());
assertTrue(diag.path("dividerSufficient").asBoolean());
assertEquals(2, diag.path("categoryCompartments").path("A").size()? — A→[1], B→[2]. size 1 each.
// unload b3
unload(pallet, "CK-U-1", List.of(b3), 201);
JsonNode history = getJson("/api/pallets/" + pallet + "/history");
assertEquals(3, history.path("events").size());
// b3 event UNLOADED with unloadedAt non-null
// occupancy freed: load b3 onto pallet2
String pallet2 = ...; createPallet(pallet2, 0, 201);
load(pallet2, "CK-L-2", items(item(b3,"B",1)), 201);
// ship pallet
MvcResult shipResult = ship(pallet, "CK-S-1", 201);
JsonNode shipBody = read(shipResult);
assertEquals(2, shipBody.path("itemCount").asInt());
assertEquals(1, shipBody.path("categoryCount").asInt());
assertEquals(1, shipBody.path("dividerVersion").asInt());
assertTrue(shipBody.path("openDurationMillis").asLong() >= 0);
// post-ship mutations forbidden
load(pallet, "CK-L-3", items(item(b1x...)), 409); — need a fresh batch; or reuse b3? b3 is on pallet2 now. Create b4 and try load → 409.
unload(pallet, "CK-U-2", List.of(b1), 409);
ship(pallet, "CK-S-2", 409);
// divider change after ship: allowed, snapshot unchanged
dividers(pallet, "CK-D-1", 5, 201);
JsonNode detail2 = getJson(...);
assertEquals(5, detail2.path("pallet").path("dividerCount").asInt());
assertEquals(2, detail2.path("pallet").path("dividerVersion").asInt());
assertEquals(1, detail2.path("shipment").path("dividerVersion").asInt());
assertEquals(2, detail2.path("shipment").path("dividerCount").asInt());
// disposal
dispose(pallet, "CK-X-1", "发现类别错误", 201);
JsonNode detail3 ... status DISPOSAL, disposal.reason
dispose(pallet, "CK-X-2", "再次", 409);
// history keeps everything: events 3 (b1 SHIPPED, b2 SHIPPED, b3 UNLOADED)
JsonNode history2 = getJson(history);
assertEquals(3, history2.path("events").size());
// verify DB: pallet_load rows intact
assertEquals(3, jdbc count pallet_load where pallet_key=pallet);
```

Wait — b3 was loaded on pallet then unloaded, then loaded on pallet2. pallet_load for pallet has 3 rows. Good.

Note detail response JSON: PalletDetailResponse fields: pallet, currentLoads, shipment, disposal. After ship, currentLoads empty (status SHIPPED). OK.

Test 2: loadValidationFailures_writeNothingAndKeyReusable
```java
String pallet = ...; createPallet(pallet, 0, 201); // 1 compartment
b1, b2, b3 batches
// insufficient dividers: two categories, two compartments needed
MvcResult r = loadRaw(pallet, body("CK-LF-1", items(item(b1,"A",1), item(b2,"B",2))), 422);
assert message contains "隔板数量不足" and "实际 0" "要求 1"
